@vaccine
# prose-audit: Grade A — Clinicians, local access and consent produce three grounded Lewica strategies with distinct public-health consequences.
title: Vaccination begins
new-page: true
on-arrival: vaccine_event_done = 1; news_headline = "Vaccination begins under conditions of scarcity"

= January 2021 — Vaccination

The first doses reach hospital freezers in a climate already poisoned by
shortages and suspicion. Doctors and nurses ask us to make the public case for
vaccination. Mayors and pharmacists answer that no Warsaw campaign matters if
older and rural patients cannot reach an appointment. Konfederacja is ready to
turn every queue, side effect rumour and delayed appointment into a story about
coercion and state collapse.

We do not control the vaccination programme. We can still decide what kind of
trust the Left lends it.

- @vaccine_public
- @vaccine_local
- @vaccine_liberty

@vaccine_public
title: Run a public-health campaign with clinicians and unions
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; vaccination_strategy = "Public-health mobilisation"; health_policy_pressure += 6; public_trust += 5; public_sector_support += 3; pandemic_deaths_pressure -= 3; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 5; konf_poll += 0.2; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Clinicians and unions lead the vaccination campaign"

Doctors, nurses and union delegates take the microphones while our MPs carry
their case into Parliament. Workplace meetings answer practical questions
more effectively than another ministerial conference. Konfederacja calls the
campaign pressure by another name, but the Left now owns a clear public-health
line—and will be judged by it if supply fails.

- @vaccine_aftershock: Face the hospital overload wave


@vaccine_local
title: Build access through councils, pharmacies and workplaces
on-arrival: vaccination_strategy = "Local access"; health_policy_pressure += 5; local_network += 3; psl_relation += 2; rural_support += 2; pandemic_deaths_pressure -= 2; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 3; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Opposition local network"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Local access becomes the vaccination argument"

Lewica councillors begin matching pharmacies, workplaces and volunteer drivers
to the gaps in the state programme. The network is uneven, but in smaller
towns it gives people a number to call and a place they recognise. PSL approves
of the localism; our organisers quietly note that an opposition party is doing
work the government should have arranged.

- @vaccine_aftershock: Face the hospital overload wave


@vaccine_liberty
title: Concentrate on voluntary consent and oversight
on-arrival: vaccination_strategy = "Consent and oversight"; constitutional_restraint += 3; health_policy_pressure += 1; konf_relation += 2; public_trust -= 2; pandemic_deaths_pressure += 4; covid_anti_system_pressure += 8; konf_braunist_share += 2; konf_mentzenite_share += 2; konf_nationalist_share -= 4; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left makes consent its vaccination line while Konfederacja recruits around it"

Our lawyers demand informed consent, published contracts and scrutiny of every
emergency measure. The safeguards deserve a hearing. So do clinicians who warn
that hesitation has a cost measured in occupied beds. Konfederacja quotes the
first half of our argument and discards the second, drawing the most suspicious
voters further into its orbit.

- @vaccine_aftershock: Face the hospital overload wave


@vaccine_aftershock
# prose-audit: Grade A — The aftershock event turns delayed care and hospital overload into a concrete public-health crisis, with each branch changing the party's credibility and the wider pandemic narrative.
title: Hospital overload and delayed care
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const trustedVaccination =
    Q.vaccination_strategy == "Public-health mobilisation" ||
    Q.vaccination_strategy == "Local access";
Q.news_headline = trustedVaccination
    ? "Vaccination trust rises, but hospitals still carry pandemic backlog"
    : "Pandemic wards and delayed care become a second crisis";
Q.pandemic_deaths_pressure += trustedVaccination ? 2 : 5;
Q.health_policy_pressure += trustedVaccination ? 2 : 1;
Q.household_policy_pressure += trustedVaccination ? 2 : 4;
Q.public_trust += trustedVaccination ? 1 : -2;
Q.covid_anti_system_pressure += trustedVaccination ? 1 : 4;
Q.story_queue = Array.isArray(Q.story_queue) ? Q.story_queue : [];
Q.story_queue.push({
    kind: "pandemic_aftershock",
    title: "Hospital overload and delayed care",
    issue: "vaccination",
    label: "Excess deaths, delayed treatment and pandemic fatigue"
});
!}

= February 2021 — The aftershock

Vaccination has begun, but ambulances still queue and non-COVID wards are full
of postponed treatment. Families who obeyed restrictions now wait months for
cardiology, oncology and mental-health care. Workers keep showing up sick
because isolation still threatens their wages.

The first pandemic emergency has become a second crisis: delayed care,
exhausted staff and households pushed into debt by illness.

- @vaccine_aftershock_staff
- @vaccine_aftershock_income
- @vaccine_aftershock_message

@vaccine_aftershock_staff
title: Demand an emergency staffing and triage package
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Highest health gain with no immediate fiscal authority.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource for national coordination.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; health_policy_pressure += 7; labor_credibility += 3; public_trust += 2; pandemic_deaths_pressure -= 3; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 2; budget_promises += 1; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Lewica makes delayed treatment the central pandemic demand"

We publish a national staffing and triage plan with clinicians and unions,
forcing every party to state how fast postponed care will be restored. The
plan does not fund itself, but it gives overwhelmed wards a concrete timetable
to fight for.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@vaccine_aftershock_income
title: Prioritise paid isolation, care leave and debt protection
subtitle: Households first; hospital backlog still grows.
on-arrival: household_policy_pressure += 7; labor_credibility += 4; public_trust += 1; pandemic_deaths_pressure += 1; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 1; budget_promises += 2; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The pandemic aftershock is framed as an income-security emergency"

We force the argument onto wages, debt and paid leave: people cannot isolate or
recover if every missed shift is a household crisis. Clinicians back the logic
while warning that a staffing answer is still missing.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@vaccine_aftershock_message
title: Keep the line optimistic and avoid new demands
subtitle: Saves resources now, deepens the credibility risk later.
on-arrival: public_trust -= 3; pandemic_deaths_pressure += 3; health_policy_pressure -= 2; household_policy_pressure -= 1; covid_anti_system_pressure += 3; konf_poll_momentum += 0.3; news_headline = "Optimistic messaging collides with overwhelmed wards"

We praise vaccination progress and decline to open another expensive policy
front. For one week the line is disciplined. Then every delayed operation and
closed local clinic becomes evidence that politics has moved on while patients
did not.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@recovery_fund
# prose-audit: Grade A — Each ratification route now has an authored Lewica aftermath naming who owns the votes, safeguards and opposition breach.
title: The EU recovery fund vote
new-page: true
on-arrival: recovery_fund_event_done = 1; news_headline = "PiS needs opposition votes for the recovery fund"

= May 2021 — Recovery fund

Poland needs the EU recovery fund, but Solidarna Polska has taken votes away
from Mateusz Morawiecki's majority. Our MPs can now secure safeguards directly,
force KO and Poland 2050 into one control package, or refuse to rescue PiS and
risk leaving the money to somebody else's arithmetic.

- @recovery_deal
- @recovery_opposition
- @recovery_abstain
- @recovery_palace

@recovery_deal
title: Negotiate safeguards with the government and vote yes
subtitle: The historical gamble.
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Negotiated PiS deal"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "Lewica yes votes complete the ratification majority"; pis_relation += 10; ko_relation -= 12; p2050_relation -= 7; relation_pis_psl += 3; rival_relation_pis_psl += 3; labor_credibility += 4; household_policy_pressure += 3; barons_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent += 5; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession"; last_policy_authority = "PiS cabinet and Sejm majority"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Lewica trades its votes for recovery-fund safeguards"

Our votes pass the law and force Morawiecki to acknowledge social and local
safeguards he did not offer freely. PiS calls us responsible; KO calls us its
lifeline. Inside Lewica, the old parliamentary wing celebrates relevance while
progressives ask who will enforce a bargain owned by the cabinet.


- @poland_hub: Continue

@recovery_opposition
title: Demand one opposition amendment slate
subtitle: Requires working relations and compatible coalition instincts.
choose-if: ko_relation >= 45 and p2050_relation >= 28 and ko_coalition_openness >= 45 and p2050_coalition_openness >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: At least one opposition partner prefers a separate strategy.
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Common opposition slate"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "A common opposition yes vote passes ratification with one control package"; ko_relation += 7; p2050_relation += 6; relation_ko_p2050 += 4; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 4; pis_relation -= 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The opposition writes one recovery-fund control package and ratifies the law"

We arrive with KO and Poland 2050 at one list of controls and vote for the money
without giving Morawiecki a private partner. The opposition proves it can
govern a common interest; PiS tells voters that three rival parties needed a
week to say yes.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@recovery_abstain
title: Refuse a bilateral deal and abstain
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Abstention"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1 if pis_seats + psl_seats >= 231; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "PiS and PSL provide the majority without Lewica" if recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "No alternative majority reaches 231" if recovery_fund_ratified = 0; pis_relation -= 2; ko_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 2; razem_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Lewica abstains and leaves ratification to the recorded PiS–PSL count"

[? if recovery_fund_ratified: PSL supplies the votes we withheld. The money
moves forward, PiS learns that another opposition partner is available, and we
own neither the safeguards nor the defeat of the government. ?]

[? if not recovery_fund_ratified: No alternative majority appears. The law
fails without our votes; Razem praises the refusal to rescue PiS while mayors
and unions ask why opposition discipline was worth delaying the fund. ?]

- @poland_hub: Continue


@recovery_palace
title: Ask Trzaskowski to sponsor and sign recovery-fund safeguards
subtitle: Cohabitation path: the President may convene, advocate and sign; Parliament and EU institutions still decide ratification and milestones.
view-if: trz_inaugurated = 1
choose-if: president_relation >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: The Palace will not guarantee a package without a working relationship.
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Presidential sponsorship"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1 if pis_seats + ko_seats + p2050_seats + psl_seats >= 231; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "A Palace-convened cross-party majority ratifies; EU institutions retain milestone control"; president_relation += 7; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 4; psl_relation += 3; pis_relation -= 5; judicial_legitimacy += 4; household_policy_pressure += 3; government_coalition_dissent += 7; trz_right_fragmentation += 10; trz_right_backlash += 5; rival_relation_pis_ko -= 4; last_policy_stage = "Presidential sponsorship"; last_policy_authority = "President may convene and sign; Sejm ratifies"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The President sponsors a recovery-fund control package for a Sejm vote"

We let President Trzaskowski convene the parties and sponsor the safeguards,
while the Sejm supplies the majority and EU institutions retain milestone
control. KO gains the photograph and we gain a package. Solidarna Polska attacks
both Morawiecki and the Palace, widening the governing fracture before the June
rights test.


- @poland_hub: Continue

@opposition_reset
# prose-audit: Grade A — KO, Poland 2050 and Lewica compete through social, democratic and local strategies with distinct organisational aftermaths.
title: The opposition resets
new-page: true
on-arrival: opposition_reset_event_done = 1; news_headline = "KO and Poland 2050 contest the same centre"

= June 2021 — Three opposition strategies

KO asks every opposition party to line up behind a single anti-PiS pole.
Szymon Hołownia presents Poland 2050 as an escape from the habits of the old
opposition and courts voters who want a new centre. Our organisers hear both
pitches as an invitation to become somebody else's left flank.

The choice is not whether to oppose PiS. It is where we intend to remain
distinct while doing it.

- @reset_social
- @reset_democratic
- @reset_local

@reset_social
title: Compete with both on wages, housing and services
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "Social competition"; labor_credibility += 5; workers_support += 3; public_sector_support += 2; ko_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 3; left_economic_position -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica opens a social flank against both centrist parties"

Our MPs take wages, rents and public services on tour while KO and Poland 2050
compete over who can best manage the centre. Both accuse us of dividing the
opposition. Trade unionists and tenants' groups hear something rarer: a reason
to support the Left that is not merely fear of PiS.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@reset_democratic
title: Rebuild the democratic-opposition table
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "Democratic opposition table"; resources -= 1; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 5; relation_ko_p2050 += 4; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; razem_dissent += 3; news_headline = "The opposition table returns with written limits"

Lawyers and parliamentary whips sit down to agree on constitutional red lines,
procedural warnings and the votes on which nobody will surprise the others.
The table gives the opposition discipline without pretending it has one
programme. Razem still fears that every shared photograph teaches voters to
see us as a junior partner in somebody else's coalition.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@reset_local
title: Leave Warsaw to the leaders and organise counties
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "County organisation"; local_network += 5; rural_support += 3; psl_relation += 3; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "County organisation replaces another leaders' summit"

The next Warsaw summit takes place without us. Our money goes instead to county
offices, bus-stop meetings and organisers looking for credible local
candidates. It produces fewer evening headlines, but more people know whom to
call when a clinic closes. PSL notices that the Left has begun treating the
counties as political ground rather than scenery between cities.

- @poland_hub: Continue


